{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1753,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You walked into the supermarket for one carton of milk.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 60
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Twenty minutes later, your cart is full and you can't remember why.",
   "from": 64,
   "to": 142
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You feel calm. The music is soft. Nobody is rushing.",
   "from": 146,
   "to": 222
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You even grabbed a bottle of French wine. You don't drink wine.",
   "from": 226,
   "to": 309
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Then a door swings open in the back. The manager is turning a dial marked tempo.",
   "from": 313,
   "to": 421
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "That soft music wasn't for you. It was for your feet.",
   "from": 436,
   "to": 521
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In nineteen eighty-two, a researcher switched a supermarket between slow and fast songs.",
   "from": 525,
   "to": 664
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "With slow music, shoppers walked slower down every aisle.",
   "from": 668,
   "to": 766
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And on slow days, sales were thirty-eight percent higher than on fast days.",
   "from": 770,
   "to": 888
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Fast songs did the opposite and hurried people along.",
   "from": 892,
   "to": 947
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Music can even pick what you buy.",
   "from": 951,
   "to": 999
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "A wine shop played French accordion music one day, German oompah the next.",
   "from": 1003,
   "to": 1110
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "On French days, seventy-seven percent of the wine sold was French.",
   "from": 1114,
   "to": 1212
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "On German days, seventy-three percent was German.",
   "from": 1216,
   "to": 1297
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Out of forty-four shoppers asked, just one mentioned the music.",
   "from": 1301,
   "to": 1393
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So the store isn't just playing songs. It's setting your speed.",
   "from": 1397,
   "to": 1492
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You finally reach the checkout with forty things and no milk.",
   "from": 1495,
   "to": 1572
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "cashier",
   "text": "Find everything you needed?",
   "from": 1576,
   "to": 1621
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Back in aisle nine, the music gets even slower.",
   "from": 1625,
   "to": 1729
  }
 ],
